<p>Unity3D Start method. </p>
<p>This method will only be called once even if multiple instances of the singleton MonoBehaviour exist in the scene. You can override this method in derived classes to customize the initialization of your MonoBehaviour </p>

<p>Reimplemented from <a class="el" href="class_mono_behaviour_singleton-1-g.html#a30ca8953ac7ddf5cbff660f599661a32">MonoBehaviourSingleton&lt; T &gt;</a>.</p>

